          "suggestions": "The only tool call evidenced in the trace is iot.sensor_stats, which correctly supports the min/max/mean table for oti, oti_a, oti_t, il1, il2, il3 and inut (values match the tool output). However, the agent never called iot.stream_extent or iot.installed_sensors to confirm the window and channels, and critically there is no iot.history call in the trace. The per-timestamp values presented (oti peak 87 °C on 2024-01-16, daily totals 300/301/299/301/300 A, oti 86 °C on Jan-18) cannot be derived from sensor_stats alone, so the timestamp-alignment conclusion appears fabricated. The agent should call iot.history for the seven sensors, compute the actual timestamp of peak oti and of peak il1+il2+il3 from retrieved rows, and only then state whether they match. The phase-imbalance calculation (no phase >10% off) is correct given the means. Also, treating ati as 'ambient' at 78 °C is an unverified interpretation; use installed_sensors metadata to confirm what ati represents."
